cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project in teaching, research, or a course, please cite it."
title: "Statistical Illusions Lab"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, open-source collection of five statistical illusions:
  Simpson's paradox, the base-rate fallacy, p-hacking, regression to the mean,
  and confidence-interval coverage. Each experiment pairs a reproducible
  simulation with an explanation of the underlying mechanism and common
  misinterpretations.
authors:
  - name: "The stat-illusions-lab contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jiezhou9/stat-illusions-lab"
keywords:
  - statistics
  - statistics education
  - data visualization
  - simulation
  - reproducibility
  - streamlit
